  "id": "COMPOUND:25477 - PROTEIN:5798",
  "verbalization": "Phaselic acid, (-)- is consistently identified as a target of NH-6 in three distinct pathways, each linking the compound to a different metabolite that ultimately targets NH-6. The evidence suggests that Phaselic acid, (-)- exerts its biological effect through a mechanism that involves the interaction with MIP, which is the target of multiple compounds, including Phlorigidoside C and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. These compounds, in turn, are all implicated in the regulation of NH-6, indicating a potential pathway where Phaselic acid, (-)- may modulate the activity of these metabolites, which in turn influence NH-6. The consistent targeting of NH-6 by Phaselic acid, (-)- across different molecular entities suggests a plausible, mechanistically coherent relationship. The presence of multiple targets for MIP and the shared pathway to NH-6 supports the idea that Phaselic acid, (-)- may act through a common or related mechanism, possibly involving the modulation of metabolic pathways or enzyme activity. The evidence is robust and aligns with the expected biological roles of these compounds, making the relationship between Phaselic acid, (-)- and NH-6 a well-supported mechanistic link.",
